# accounts.encrypted.json (Example Structure)

This file is automatically generated and encrypted by the Account Manager.
Do NOT edit this file manually - use the web interface instead.

## File Location
`accounts.encrypted.json` - Stored in the root bot directory
`.encryption-key` - Encryption key for token decryption (chmod 600)

## Example (Decrypted Structure)
```json
{
  "mybot": {
    "name": "mybot",
    "clientId": "abcd1234efgh5678",
    "clientSecret": "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
    "broadcasterName": "mytwitch",
    "channels": ["mytwitch", "friendstream"],
    "accessToken": "encrypted...access_token...",
    "refreshToken": "encrypted...refresh_token...",
    "tokenScopes": ["chat:read", "chat:edit", "clips:edit"],
    "broadcasterAccessToken": "encrypted...broadcaster_token...",
    "broadcasterRefreshToken": "encrypted...broadcaster_refresh...",
    "broadcasterScopes": ["moderator:read:followers", "channel:read:redemptions"],
    "createdAt": "2026-01-19T10:30:00.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-01-19T11:45:00.000Z",
    "tokenExpiresAt": "2026-01-20T10:30:00.000Z",
    "broadcasterTokenExpiresAt": "2026-01-20T11:45:00.000Z"
  },
  "testbot": {
    "name": "testbot",
    "clientId": "xyz9876abcd1234",
    "clientSecret": "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy",
    "broadcasterName": "testchannel",
    "channels": ["testchannel"],
    "accessToken": "encrypted...",
    "refreshToken": "encrypted...",
    "tokenScopes": ["chat:read", "chat:edit"],
    "broadcasterAccessToken": null,
    "broadcasterRefreshToken": null,
    "broadcasterScopes": [],
    "createdAt": "2026-01-10T14:20:00.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-01-19T09:00:00.000Z",
    "tokenExpiresAt": "2026-01-20T14:20:00.000Z",
    "broadcasterTokenExpiresAt": null
  }
}
```

## Security Notes

- ✅ All tokens are encrypted with AES-256-CBC
- ✅ Encryption key is stored separately in `.encryption-key`
- ✅ File permissions are restricted to owner-only (0o600)
- ✅ DO NOT commit `.encryption-key` to version control
- ✅ If lost, encryption key cannot be recovered - tokens will be inaccessible

## Account Management via Web UI

1. Open `http://localhost:3000`
2. Navigate to "Account Manager" tab
3. Create new account with OAuth credentials
4. Click "Authorize Bot" or "Authorize Broadcaster"
5. Tokens are automatically encrypted and saved

## Account Management via CLI

```bash
# View account manager module usage
node -e "const AM = require('./account-manager'); const am = new AM(); console.log(am.listAccounts())"

# Export account as .env
node -e "const AM = require('./account-manager'); const am = new AM(); console.log(am.exportToEnv('mybot'))"
```

## Starting Bot with Specific Account

```bash
node Excella --account=mybot
node Excella --account=testbot
```

## Emergency Recovery

If encryption key is lost:
1. Delete `accounts.encrypted.json` and `.encryption-key`
2. A new key will be generated on next token-generator start
3. Re-authorize all accounts through the UI
